-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner involution on X₁(Mp) over ℚ(ζₚ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ which is assumed equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (the map induced on Laurent series by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $j \in K$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the expansion $q^{-1}\prod$-type series $\mathrm{single}(-1,1)\cdot \mathrm{ofPowerSeries}(j\mathrm{NumQ})$ of the modular $j$-invariant. Then there exists an $L$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ with two properties. First, the Laurent series underlying $\sigma(j)$ is the image of [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), the series obtained from $j(q)$ by multiplying all exponents by $p$, i.e. $j(q^p)$. Second, for every element $f$ of [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305) — the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated by the series $j(q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $Mp$ — whose image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) lies in $K$, the value of $\sigma$ at that image is the image of [`ModularCurve.atkinLehnerInvolutionFull M p f`](def/ModularCurve_AtkinLehnerPartial.html#L21), where `atkinLehnerInvolutionFull M p` is a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of that field interchanging $j(q^d)$ and $j(q^{dp})$ for every nonzero divisor $d$ of $M$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ at the prime $p$ exactly dividing the level $Mp$ is realised, after base change to a $p$-th cyclotomic field, by an automorphism of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ sending $j(q)$ to $j(q^p)$ and acting on the subfield generated by the $j(q^d)$, $d \mid Mp$, as the divisor-swapping involution. It is used by the strengthened version of the same existence result, which adds information about charts and about the behaviour of the automorphism under comparison maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_algEquiv_map_j_eq_qExpand_and_coe_eq_atkinLehnerInvolutionFull_x1_mul.lean

import Mathlib
